LinkedList Big O
1. Inserting at the end of LL means have to update tail with new node, no need of iteration so it will be O(1)
2. Removing at the end of LL means have to update to last 2nd node for that we have to iterate over LL and the update tail
  with that last 2nd node,  so it will be O(n)
3. Inserting and Removing at the start of LL means have to update head to new node or next node, no need of iteration 
  so it will be O(1)
4. searching/finding by index, removing/ adding at the middle of LL means iteration required so it will be O(n)
